# Independent checked-site payload and CI review

Decision: approved after one small format-validation correction; no remaining blocking finding in this payload-only scope. Reviewed tools/site/payload.py,test_payload.py, .github/workflows/ci.yml, doc/development.md and original spec15 distribution/recovery requirements. Initial checkpoint99d4307 was subsequently merged with main at c7747ad963e289b58ac091beab609b8358f7641e; reviewed final version includes the uncommitted strict-version correction. No production edits made by reviewer.

Initial finding: version comparison ==1 accepted JSON true and1.0. Independently reproduced both successful malformed-version packages; version-repro.json preserves the failure evidence. Root now requires a manifest object and exactly integer1, with five regression inputs true/1.0/string1/null/2. Independently ran final7 tests in ordinary Python and with -O: both pass. No asserts protect production validation, so optimization does not disable checks. Tests exercise exact/over byte counts, file/entry bounds, an actual Windows junction, scan errors, hard links, stale digest/modified/missing/unlisted/duplicate/traversal inputs, output containment/existing output, deterministic member bytes and normalized metadata. The previously addressed junction/scan-error paths were also read directly.

Independent real-artifact execution uses the actual browser report digest for .tmp/site-final-primary. Packed twice into fresh files, inspected all22 tar members against exact original file bytes, checked sorted names, regular members only, mode0644, zero mtime/uid/gid and empty owner names. Both tar byte streams and receipts are identical. Final corrected packer produced a third identical tar. Result:1,177,600 bytes; SHA256 cc053272f49f8d4d79fc756560df5401bfdc22b8c1e1a1177ae0250cdc265cd9. The input manifest SHA256 is39000dd5b7aad48deae97741c5b077b44a242a0badb7b30e81b3c1c26f301446. results.json retains this evidence. These are prior checked site bytes, intentionally independent of the later packaging-code commit; they are not a claim of a fresh site build at c7747ad.

The packer requires the externally supplied checked digest, rejects linked ancestors/directories and linked/special/multilink files, propagates enumeration/read failures, binds opened files to examined file identity, and verifies exact manifest membership/length/hash before tar output. Only frozen in-memory bytes enter tarfile; subsequent filesystem changes cannot replace archived bytes. Path rules reject traversal, platform-special names and case-colliding prefixes. Input sizes/counts and tar overhead have finite bounds. Output is exclusive and outside the input site. Validation failures occur before output creation; an actual output I/O failure propagates and may leave an incomplete output, but cannot return a success receipt or pass CI.

CI sequencing is correct: both existing site/browser checks must succeed before the payload step runs, digest is read from the successful primary browser report, and root site bytes are not regenerated between check and pack. Bash/step failures propagate; no continue-on-error or publication permissions are added. The tar, outer receipt and original site/report share the existing doc-browser artifact. Tests run on the three native OS jobs and the browser job; the Windows-only junction test explicitly skips elsewhere. Existing quality dependency still requires those jobs. Packaging currently applies to primary base; alternate remains independently browser-checked and retained, not falsely claimed packaged.

Spec15 distinguishes checked artifacts from actual publication and public-smoke/LKG evidence. Development docs and publication_verified:false preserve this distinction. This normal Actions artifact is a retained candidate tar, not an executed upload-pages-artifact/deploy-pages transaction, a persistent immutable recovery release, freshness lock, public smoke or LKG. Their later integration remains required. No full T19/T20/T21/runtime completion or deployed Pages compatibility test is inferred here.

git diff --check passes. Reviewed file snapshots are included with this independent record. Final GitHub CI at the completed PR head remains a separate integration gate; this reviewer did not rerun workspace Rust or live publication checks.

Final commit follow-up: all four reviewed file snapshots exactly match committed0c12e9c. Re-executed the final7 tests under normal Python and -O against that commit, both pass; commands.json and separate raw stdout/stderr logs retain the invocation and results. PR106 CI remains separately pending.
